ig's cost: ~30 calls of hunting for a file that the record\nclaimed existed. The lesson is not \"records lie\" -- it's that a\nrecord entry about WHERE something lives is itself an unverified\nclaim. Next time a filing cites a file path, the first move is\ntest -f, not find.\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org 2\u003e/dev/null; IAR_ALLOW_TAIL=1 git commit -m \"aria c59: journal entry (credentials archaeology)\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1; git push origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:19:08.50923885Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T14:19:08.588772024Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":4907356022,"prompt_eval_count":62533,"prompt_eval_cached_count":53760,"eval_count":555}\n(9594ae80653bef15797a279a2012507b . 648)
