master today: `Conn.AddTrack` in the ModeActiveProducer branch still hits `if c.state == StatePlay { c.Reconnect() }` unconditionally, with no check against existing `c.Senders`. Also re-verified that commit fde1fdc5 (recent rtsp refactor) touched `consumer.go` but did not touch this path -- the asymmetry with `Conn.GetTrack`'s pointer-equality receiver dedup (`pkg/rtsp/producer.go`) is unchanged.\n\n**3. New: the blast radius is worse than a 20s stall -- consumers can wedge.**\n\nA single-probe reproducer (one `GET /api/streams?src=<cam>&video=all&audio=all&microphone=`, no page load) remade the producer's RTSP session as expected. But on the remade session the downstream frigate recorder did not just stall -- it entered a restart loop for ~3 minutes (`No frames received in 20 seconds` x3+, ending in `vf#1 Function not implemented -> Nothing was written`) and never self-healed. It took a go2rtc stream reload (DELETE+PUT on `/api/streams?src=<cam>`) to recover. So on some consumer/codec combinations the probe doesn't cost 20s of downtime, it costs a manual intervention. This strengthens the case for direction (a) -- dedup in `Conn.AddTrack` against existing senders -- since the probe buys the requester nothing (the metadata response is identical without the reconnect).\n\nHappy to test a patch or provide more logs (full producer remake timeline, ffmpeg restart-loop logs) if useful.\nEOF\nwc -c /tmp/gh_comment.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[14:33:47] 2210 /tmp/gh_comment.md\n\n[t+01:48/60:00 c10/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_fbyjmsrd","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"TOK=$(cat /tmp/gh_token); RESP=$(curl -s --max-time 25 -X POST -H \"Authorization: token $TOK\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \"https://api.github.com/repos/AlexxIT/go2rtc/issues/2505/comments\" -d \"$(jq -Rs '{body: .}' < /tmp/gh_comment.md)\"); echo \"$RESP\" | jq -r '{id: .id, url: .html_url, created: .created_